 ## Honest ceiling
 
-AnonSync is the product. The current package is still a local C++ library/CLI and deterministic harness. It is **not yet** a production peer discovery system, LAN/WAN/NAT traversal layer, encrypted peer protocol, file watcher, persistent manifest database, chunk transfer engine, partial-transfer/resume engine, mobile/desktop daemon, or privacy-preserving distributed sync deployment. Rev0659 can scan live local files into manifests, plan local/remote reconciliation, turn that reconciliation into local filesystem intents, materialize a fully staged remote file after verification, reject stale local target overwrites, execute remote tombstones against regular files after stale-target preflight, and preserve regular local files as conflict copies before applying a conflicting remote file or tombstone. The next code-bearing revision should add chunk receipt/write accounting or persisted manifest/index state.
+AnonSync is the product. The current package is still a local C++ library/CLI and deterministic harness. It is **not yet** a production peer discovery system, LAN/WAN/NAT traversal layer, encrypted peer protocol, file watcher, persistent manifest database, chunk transfer scheduler, mobile/desktop daemon, or privacy-preserving distributed sync deployment. Rev0660 can scan live local files into manifests, plan local/remote reconciliation, turn that reconciliation into local filesystem intents, receive and receipt individual remote chunks into staging, detect complete staged files, materialize verified remote files, reject stale local target overwrites, execute remote tombstones against regular files, and preserve regular local files as conflict copies before applying a conflicting remote file or tombstone. The next code-bearing revision should add cleanup of orphaned receipt/staging directories, persisted transfer state, or a fake peer-session harness that drives these APIs end-to-end.
