diff --git a/cpp/anonsync_core/README.md b/cpp/anonsync_core/README.md
index eae8ff6..d3bbce1 100644
--- a/cpp/anonsync_core/README.md
+++ b/cpp/anonsync_core/README.md
@@ -1,8 +1,8 @@
-# anonsync_core rev0659
+# anonsync_core rev0660
 
 `anonsync_core` is the C++20 working library for AnonSync, a peer-to-peer file synchronization system. The target product is Resilio Sync-style folder replication across authorized devices, with content identity, resumable transfer, crash-safe local state, conflict handling, and authenticated peer/session boundaries.
 
-Rev0659 extends the sync-domain module introduced in rev0651, folder-manifested in rev0652, connected to deterministic local directory scanning in rev0653, reconciled by manifest diff planning in rev0654, turned into local apply plans in rev0655, given verified staged-file materialization in rev0656, hardened with stale-target preflight in rev0657, and extended with remote tombstone application in rev0658:
+Rev0660 extends the sync-domain module introduced in rev0651, folder-manifested in rev0652, connected to deterministic local directory scanning in rev0653, reconciled by manifest diff planning in rev0654, turned into local apply plans in rev0655, given verified staged-file materialization in rev0656, hardened with stale-target preflight in rev0657, extended with remote tombstone application in rev0658, and extended with conflict-copy preservation in rev0659:
 
 - `NormalizedSyncPath` and `normalize_sync_relative_path` for portable relative path policy;
 - `SyncManifestEntry`, `SyncChunkRange`, and `SyncVersionLineageEntry` for file/tombstone entry identity;
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@ Rev0659 extends the sync-domain module introduced in rev0651, folder-manifested
 - `SyncFolderScanOptions` and `build_sync_folder_manifest_from_directory` for deterministic local directory indexing;
 - `SyncPlanAction`, `SyncLineageRelation`, `SyncManifestPlanEntry`, and `SyncManifestDiffPlan` for local/remote reconciliation planning, carrying local/remote size and content-hash evidence;
 - `SyncLocalApplyAction`, `SyncLocalApplyOptions`, `SyncLocalApplyPlanEntry`, and `SyncLocalApplyPlan` for safe local filesystem intent planning, carrying local/remote presence, kind, size, content, digest, and version evidence;
+- `SyncChunkReceiptWriteOptions` and `SyncChunkReceiptWriteResult` for receipt-backed staged chunk writes and resume evidence;
 - `SyncStagedFileMaterializationOptions` and `SyncStagedFileMaterializationResult` for verified staged-file commit evidence, including stale-target preflight flags;
 - `SyncTombstoneApplicationOptions` and `SyncTombstoneApplicationResult` for safe remote tombstone application evidence;
 - `SyncConflictPreservationOptions` and `SyncConflictPreservationResult` for safe conflict-copy preservation evidence;
@@ -20,74 +21,23 @@ Rev0659 extends the sync-domain module introduced in rev0651, folder-manifested
 - `sync_folder_manifest_digest` for stable folder-manifest identity;
 - `build_sync_manifest_diff_plan` for fetch/publish/tombstone/conflict/no-op planning between two peer manifests;
 - `build_sync_local_apply_plan` for mapping diff entries to staged remote files, local deletes, conflict-copy preservation, and outbound peer advertisements;
-- `materialize_staged_sync_file` for verifying a complete staged remote file against manifest chunk/content hashes, preflighting the current local target, fsyncing, and atomically renaming it into the local folder;
-- `apply_sync_remote_tombstone` for verifying a remote tombstone apply intent, preflighting the current local target, deleting only the planned regular file, fsyncing the target directory, and emitting `sync-tombstone:v1:` evidence;
