-## Rev0659 sync-domain policy
-
-Rev0659 executes the conflict-copy local mutation for planned regular local files. The boundary is intentionally conservative: a conflict plan is not trusted after time has passed unless the current target still matches the plan's local evidence.
-
-For `apply_sync_conflict_preservation`:
-
-- the remote entry must validate as a file or tombstone;
-- the apply entry must be `RecordConflict` mapped to `PreserveConflictCopy`;
-- the remote entry digest and publisher-neutral version digest must match the apply entry;
-- a planned local regular file, local size, local SHA-256, conflict set id, and deterministic conflict-copy path are required;
-- the target path and conflict-copy path must stay under the local root and must not cross symlink ancestors;
-- the current target must be a regular file whose size and SHA-256 match the planned local evidence before the conflict copy is made;
-- an existing conflict-copy path is accepted only if it is a regular file whose content already matches the planned local evidence;
-- for remote file conflicts, the staged remote file must match manifest chunk/content hashes before the remote version is promoted to the target path;
-- for remote tombstone conflicts, the local file is copied first and then the original target is removed;
-- the target is preflighted again after local copy preservation and before the remote file/tombstone is applied.
-
-This still covers only conflicts with a planned regular local file. Local tombstone vs remote file conflict semantics, partial transfers, persisted conflict metadata, and UI-facing conflict policy remain future work.
